  "limitations": [
    "Native measurements cover isolated idle helper processes, not total app CPU or energy. Baseline CPU is already only about 0.006% of one CPU; zero candidate CPU/wakeups is the observation in these bounded windows, not a universal zero-use guarantee.",
    "No meaningful memory improvement is established: candidate mean physical footprint is 12288 bytes higher per helper in these windows; kernel queue resources and one extra descriptor are a tradeoff. RSS and physical footprint differ.",
    "The retained app check is one startup-only candidate run with common compiled Swift/resources and new canonical Rust. It is a launch/identity check and prioritization sample, not a matched app-wide performance comparison.",
    "The six app-owned diagnostic samples repeat latest tick values between refreshes and measure elapsed phases, not phase CPU. Existing adaptive target cadence varies; the app observations do not identify the unmeasured tick time or establish its cause.",
    "No new compiler speed claim is made. The warm canonical pipeline reuses the tested shipping helper and validates both passes21/22 together; normal release tests, strict all-target Clippy and formatting pass.",
    "Hosted CI at the baseline commit fails dependency-policy preflight before compilation. Local validation does not replace the hosted gate; the policy is unchanged."
  ],
